[{:seon.task/name "a-branch-head-is-a-store-a-render-derefs"
  :seon.task/plan "Web's (agreed with context-4, 2026-11-14), after the reaction core lands.\n\nShape: a branch's head is (seon.ratom/store db) per branch, kept by the render proc, which owns its reads. Its commit! is fed by that branch's commit notices (seon.writer/a-branch-commit-sends-its-datoms, runtime's). It is the same Store and the same key-set match as main's, with no second mechanism.\n\nA component that derefs a branch's store records that branch's datom keys and re-runs only on that branch's commits that touch them.\n\nDeletes: the render proc's ask-turns, turns! and branch-turn, and the {:op :branch-db} asks for turns. seon.render.ui/turns-tile draws my.root/turns-of's rows by deref, so the turns ledger is one implementation in two views.\n\nUsers: the turns tile, and seon.render.ui/roots-page-shows-each-branchs-drift-from-main.\n\nEstimate: a branch commit costs its datoms matched against the readers' key sets (O(datoms moved)). No branch head is read whole, and nothing is asked.\n\nProof: seon.render-test/a-component-reading-a-branch-reruns-on-its-commit. It reruns on a commit of a datom it read on branch b, not on one of branch c, and not on b's commit of a datom it didn't read.\n\nCatch-up [M]: the branch Store reuses advance-main's rule as is (render/proc.clj:852-865). On each notice it reads the head at :commit, diffs from the head it holds (ctx/moved, O(changed)), and calls commit! with those datoms. A db no newer changes nothing. A dropped notice is covered by the next one's diff, so the Store never reads :ops."
  :seon.task/kind :whole
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/a-component-reading-a-branch-reruns-on-its-commit}
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.writer/a-branch-commit-sends-its-datoms"}}]